abstract: "Exact three-state, two-bath counterexamples with local detailed balance to Ptaszynski's 2022 conjectures that C3/C1 and C4/C2 of the heat current are nonnegative; both ratios tend to minus infinity at fixed thermodynamic data; two states never suffice in the standard model; variance-normalised ratios stay finite in the trap family and variance-based bounds are untouched; six states make even normalised ratios unbounded; a kinetic bound for C1, C2 > 0. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text and data CC0-1.0; code MIT."
